{
  "name": "rose-chafer",
  "_about": "The rose chafer (Cetonia aurata), 1.8 cm long: broad-shouldered and flat-topped, the wing cases narrowing behind, brilliant metallic golden-green, a few small white cross-marks on their back half; a trapezoid pronotum, a small head with a short three-leaved antennal club; coppery-green legs, the tarsi long. It flies with its wing cases closed. Written whole by tools/creaturegen/rework/insects/beetles.py on insectlib.py (six jointed legs on a tripod gait, the antennae on bones of their own that wave).",
